  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper proposes a gate-based variational QFDNN for two finance tasks: credit card fraud detection and loan eligibility prediction. On the CCF dataset it reports 0.822 accuracy, 0.9524 precision, and 0.8779 recall; on the LP dataset it reports 0.744 accuracy, 0.7659 precision, and 0.8932 recall, using a 3-qubit circuit with COBYLA over 10 iterations and noisy simulation across six noise models. Classical baselines are stronger overall, reaching 1.000 accuracy on CCF (RF/GB) and 0.854 on LP (LR/SVM).",
